{"availability":"available","full":"alexanderantonov/tinkerapp","name":"tinkerapp","description":"Offline 3D editor for 3D printing in a single HTML file under 2 MB. Inspired by Tinkercad; no installation or server required.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-16T16:46:34Z","updated":"2026-10-01T17:37:56Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alexanderantonov.github.io/tinkerapp/tinkerapp.html","topics":["3d-modeling","3d-printing","browser-based","cad","html","javascript","offline","single-file","stl","webgl"],"demo":"https://alexanderantonov.github.io/tinkerapp/tinkerapp.html","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.809Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.809Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.809Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.809Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I love Tinkercad, but it needs an internet connection. I wanted something I could use offline, so I built TinkerApp: a tiny 3D editor inspired by Tinkercad, packed into a single HTML file under 2 MB.","For offline use, download the HTML file and open it in your browser. No installation, no server, no internet needed. Use it on a PC or tablet, across operating systems, with a modern browser that supports WebGL."],"features":["Basic shapes, text, and screw threads for designing models for 3D printing.","Move, resize, rotate, align, mirror, and combine shapes or cut holes.","Import and export STL files.","Automatically save your five most recent projects in your browser’s local database.","Save editable projects as files and open them again on another device."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexanderantonov/tinkerapp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8be3721bc5549df9fecad7e52b16e7d6ba13ad5b7b526752e8de6f3e723f1962","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:04.545Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:04.545Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoe